i'm delighted to welcome so many leaders  here from right across the world  basically you represent not only the  diversity of the world  but also the diversity of democracies  because each of our democracies is  different and unique  but ultimately  democracy in all its forms  comes down to the same thing  it gives people a voice  it gives the ability to change things at  the ballot box  in democracies we even fight for people  to be able to be against us  to be able to speak their mind to change  their mind  to be free to be yourself  so that if you're different from the  majority you are always equal before the  law  it is the accountability to all not only  to those who voted for you and that is  democracy  a system where power is given  and taken away by citizens  and framed by checks and balances  so our debate today will be about  drawing on each other's experience to  help strengthen our democracies  here in europe we have learned that we  must always every single day nurture  and work on improving democracy  because we know how quickly and how  devastatingly  history can change  we know that the opponents of democracy  today  are using new tools and very modern  technologies  to oppress and manipulate through  systematic disinformation  this information is not a party  political issue it is a societal one  we know also that autocracy can even be  born from within democracy  and its poison can take over by misusing  institutions and democratic openness  to gradually shut down opposition curb  freedoms and to finally impose one  autocratic vision of society  we will not let that happen  and this is why the european union and  its member states are the biggest global  donor  in the area of democracy support  we will allocate 1.5 billion euros to  promote human rights and to foster  democracy globally  beyond this our global gateway strategy  will unleash 300 billion euros for  infrastructure investments around the  world  infrastructure  that is based on values on transparency  and on sustainability  to really give an alternative  and we have also put forward measure to  help measures to help protect people  from illegal content online  from hidden political advertising or  disinformation  we want to work with our partners to  ensure  that digital technologies are driven by  the values which our societies are built  on  i think that today's discussion has  shown how colorful democracy is  and how we all use different words and  pictures to describe what it means to us  and to the people we serve  we have seen just how vibrant democracy  is around the world and just how strong  the commitment is to strengthen it  common understanding that democracy can  and must deliver for people we all face  many of the same challenges  how to promote greater participation  how to protect free press from fake news  and disinformation  how to root out corruption and  strengthen the rule of law  we all know and that was very  interesting to hear it in different  voices that democracy is imperfect by  design and imperfect in reality  but there's also a common will to  reinforce democracy  as the fairest way to deliver the  greatest benefits to people around the  world  to create societies that are equal  and allow opportunities to all  so today's session  is not the end of something it is the  beginning  of a new push for democracy
 

